{
  "_id": "agent-flight-recorder-charter",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "block-0",
      "text": "Goal charter · agent flight recorder",
      "type": "eyebrow"
    },
    {
      "id": "block-1",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "The agent flight recorder: primed, signed, recoverable",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "id": "block-2",
      "items": [
        "see how every agent was primed, start and finish",
        "crash → return to initial state + review instruction",
        "every action signed by a specific agent, not 'agents'"
      ],
      "type": "byline"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "1."
            }
          ],
          "type": "strong"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " Every task claim stores a PRIMING MANIFEST (what exactly the agent started with — artifacts by hash); every close stores a self-written /compact of the session (~$0.10, measured). "
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "2."
            }
          ],
          "type": "strong"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " A lapsed lease with no close = presumed crash; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "bp task resume"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " rebuilds the initial loadout from the manifest + injects the crash brief (last pulse now-line, partial-work pointers, 'review before continuing'). "
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "3."
            }
          ],
          "type": "strong"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " Every mutation carries a minted per-agent identity — history shows WHICH agent did what. All three ride existing seams; no new infrastructure."
        }
      ],
      "id": "block-3",
      "title": "TL;DR",
      "tone": "info",
      "type": "callout"
    },
    {
      "id": "block-4",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Pillar 1 — priming visibility (start + done)",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "header": [
        "Moment",
        "What is stored",
        "Where",
        "Cost (measured)"
      ],
      "id": "block-5",
      "rows": [
        [
          [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "claim"
                }
              ],
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "priming manifest: brief digest, primer artifacts by content-hash (atlas pages, doc-tier map, epic map), model+effort, worktree/branch/HEAD, memory files list, env dialect"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "task doc field priming_start (~1-2 KB)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "~free — assembled from what the spawner already knows"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "pulse"
                }
              ],
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "now-line + lease renew (exists today — task.pulse)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "mutation_events"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "existing"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "close"
                }
              ],
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "context_compact: the agent's self-written session summary as its closing act (context already in-window → output tokens only) + final HEAD/PR refs"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "task doc field (~15 KB)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "~$0.10 Opus / $0.06 Sonnet per close; 15 MB per 1,000 tasks"
            }
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Why hashes, not prose: "
            }
          ],
          "type": "strong"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "the duel judges docked an error-free primer solely because its pages could not be verified against source. A manifest of content-hashes makes priming REPRODUCIBLE (rebuild the exact loadout) and AUDITABLE (prove what the agent saw). Caveat from the compact research: a /compact is editorial at ~52× — the tail is gone, not blurred — so the manifest points at artifacts; the compact narrates. Optionally archive the flattened transcript (800 KB, object storage, grep-able) as the lossless layer — pending the compact-vs-optical verdict."
        }
      ],
      "id": "block-6",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "id": "block-7",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Pillar 2 — crash recovery",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "claim ──▶ priming_start stored ──▶ work (pulse now-lines) ──▶ close: compact stored\n                                        │\n                                        ▼ lease lapses, no close/release\n                       ttl_sweeper: task.lease_expired  (exists today)\n                                        │\n                                        ▼\n        bp task resume <id> <worker>  (NEW)\n        ├─ rebuilds the initial loadout from priming_start (same artifacts, by hash)\n        ├─ injects the CRASH BRIEF: prior agent identity + epoch, its LAST PULSE\n        │  now-line ('what it was doing when it died'), worktree/branch/PR pointers\n        └─ instruction: REVIEW partial work first — continue or reset, never re-do blind"
        }
      ],
      "id": "block-8",
      "type": "terminal"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Detection is already built"
            }
          ],
          "type": "strong"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " (lease_expired rows, ttl_sweeper). The new verbs: storing the manifest at claim, and "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "task resume"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " assembling manifest + crash brief. The crash-recovery memory from 2026-07-09 documents exactly this need — recovery today is manual archaeology."
        }
      ],
      "id": "block-9",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "id": "block-10",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Pillar 3 — signatures: who did what, not 'agents did things'",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "header": [
        "Level",
        "Mechanism",
        "Ships"
      ],
      "id": "block-11",
      "rows": [
        [
          [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "v1 · attribution"
                }
              ],
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "agent identity minted at claim (name + session id + task + epoch), threaded through every mutation as actor — server-stamped, not self-reported free-form worker strings. Ledger already exists (mutation_events, audit-emit); the gap is only the identity field discipline."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "wave 1"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "v2 · receipts"
                }
              ],
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "per-agent HMAC key minted at claim (the ticket-key mint/rotate/pause pattern, reused verbatim) signs each event row → tamper-evident per-agent history"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "wave 2, only if v1 proves insufficient"
            }
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Query surface: "
            }
          ],
          "type": "strong"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "bp task history <id>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " = per-agent timeline of one task; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "bp agent history <name>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " = one agent's actions across all tasks. Both are reads over the existing ledger once actor is disciplined."
        }
      ],
      "id": "block-12",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "id": "block-13",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Decisions to make (the epic's Decide phase)",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "id": "block-14",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "D1 manifest schema"
              }
            ],
            "type": "strong"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — which fields are mandatory; hash algorithm; where oversized artifacts live (task doc vs linked artifact doc vs object storage)."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "D2 compact-on-close policy"
              }
            ],
            "type": "strong"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — mandatory for all closes or opt-in per priority; which rubric (the /compact nine-section shape measured at 51.9× vs a task-scoped shorter one)."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "D3 resume semantics"
              }
            ],
            "type": "strong"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — does resume re-claim (new epoch) automatically; how many crash cycles before escalation; interaction with the pr-task-gate."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "D4 identity minting"
              }
            ],
            "type": "strong"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — who mints (server at claim vs spinner at spawn); collision rules with existing free-form worker strings; migration."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "D5 archive layer"
              }
            ],
            "type": "strong"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — flattened transcript stored per close (800 KB) or on-demand only; ruled by the compact-vs-optical experiment verdict."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "id": "block-15",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Measured costs (from the flight-recorder costing, 2026-07-17)",
